    "deep": "A digital product passport is a set of product data made accessible through the mechanism or standard used by a target market or programme. Define product identity, composition, origin, care instructions, repair information and end-of-life data as required. Verify authenticity, update status and sharing rights; a QR code alone is not a complete passport.\n\n**Scope and input-data analysis.** “Digital Product Passports and Product Data” should be assessed against rules tied to the intended use. Completeness means that all fields needed for a decision are present; accuracy means that values match an authoritative source; consistency means that the same entity does not conflict across systems; validity means that values conform to the required format and domain; uniqueness means that no duplicate records exist under the key; and timeliness means that data arrives before the decision is made. A field may be syntactically valid yet operationally wrong—for example, a delivery date may be in the future but still conflict with the buyer’s confirmed schedule.\n\n**Operating design and control points.** Create a rule catalogue containing the rule name, applicable field, logic, severity, reference source, execution frequency, owner and action when the rule fails. Classify errors as transaction-blocking, warnings requiring confirmation, or issues that can be corrected in batches. Track both the error rate and the number of affected records so that a low percentage does not conceal a critical group of orders. Apply checks where data is created and where it is consumed; detecting an issue only on a dashboard usually makes correction more expensive.\n\n**Reconciliation, exception handling and evidence.** Manage issues by error code and cause: incorrect entry, faulty mapping, unclear rules, defective source data, failed synchronization or a process change. Retain before-and-after snapshots, the approver and the impact on reports already issued. Review recurring errors periodically and correct their systemic causes instead of manually cleaning data every month. When a metric has not reached the required reliability, display a warning and restrict its use rather than presenting it as an official figure.\n\n**Applied exercise:** Use a garment-enterprise scenario with a specific style code, PO, factory, materials and delivery milestones. For “Digital Product Passports and Product Data”, map the data or process flow and identify the authoritative source, revision, owner, approval rights, exceptions and evidence to retain. Create at least two failure scenarios (one data failure and one operational failure), then describe detection, containment, root cause, corrective action and effectiveness verification. Distinguish verified facts from assumptions; do not invent legal limits or technical thresholds where no applicable control requirement has been specified.",
    "diagram": "<figure class=\"phase20-diagram\" style=\"margin:18px 0;padding:12px;border:1px solid #d7e0e7;border-radius:14px;background:#fff;overflow-x:auto\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 770 160\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Digital Product Passports and Product Data\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;min-width:620px;height:auto\"><title>Digital Product Passports and Product Data</title><text x=\"14\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#29364f\">Digital Product Passports and Product Data</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#617586\">Data flow, responsibilities and control points</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"76\" width=\"164\" height=\"66\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eef1f7\" stroke=\"#5b6e91\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#29364f\">Boundary</text><path d=\"M180 109 h18 m-6 -6 l6 6 -6 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b36b35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"76\" width=\"164\" height=\"66\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eef1f7\" stroke=\"#5b6e91\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#29364f\">Activity data</text><path d=\"M374 109 h18 m-6 -6 l6 6 -6 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b36b35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><rect x=\"402\" y=\"76\" width=\"164\" height=\"66\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eef1f7\" stroke=\"#5b6e91\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"484\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#29364f\">Calculation</text><path d=\"M568 109 h18 m-6 -6 l6 6 -6 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b36b35\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><rect x=\"596\" y=\"76\" width=\"164\" height=\"66\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#eef1f7\" stroke=\"#5b6e91\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#29364f\">Disclosure</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"157\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#617586\">Measure outcomes using data with a clear source and owner.</text></svg></figure>"
